  "description": "A vulnerability was detected in Portabilis i-Educar up to 2.10. This affects an unknown function of the file /intranet/agenda.php of the component Agenda Module. Performing a manipulation of the argument cod_agenda results in sql injection. It is possible to initiate the attack remotely. The exploit is now public and may be used. Upgrading to version 2.12 mitigates this issue. It is suggested to upgrade the affected component. The vendor confirms: \"The reported attack vector was tested against the corrected code, and the previously described SQL Injection behavior could no longer be reproduced.\"",
